# Prolog, program 1 hanoi_moves, the stops walk: developer_05 2026-11-23. One breakpoint at line 3 of cell 1 (M is N - 1, the body goal of the recursive clause), cell 2 run, then Continue to the end: the program makes seven calls with N above 0, so seven stops, in the order of the calls (a pre-order of the recursion, worked out from the program: left to right through hanoi(N-1, ...), record, hanoi(N-1, ...)); the output is the moves written before each stop. Frames top first as [name/arity, line of the waiting call].
